.TH TANGSIBLE-HOSTS 1 "August 2026" "Tangsible" "Tangsible Manual"
.SH NAME
tangsible-hosts \- browse every inventory host
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tangsible hosts
.RI [ playbook.yml ]
.RI [ "ansible\-playbook args" ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B hosts
lists every host reported by
.B ansible\-inventory \-\-list
(alphabetically), and opens the same five\-tab detail view
.BR tangsible-host (1)
shows for whichever one you select \(em without needing to know a
hostname up front. If
.I playbook.yml
is omitted, it is resolved the same way as
.BR tangsible-run (1)
(see
.BR tangsible (1)).
.SH KEY BINDINGS
.TP
.B "Cursor keys / j\-k"
Move the selection in the list.
.TP
.B Enter
Open the selected host's detail view.
.TP
.B Esc
From the detail view, clears an active search if there is one; otherwise
goes back to the list.
.TP
.B n / N
From the detail view, switch to the next / previous host in the list,
keeping the currently active tab.
.TP
.B Tab / Shift\-Tab
Switch tabs within the detail view.
.TP
.B /
Search the active tab's text; while a search is active,
.B n / N
jump to the next / previous match instead of the next / previous host.
.TP
.B Ctrl\-A / Ctrl\-E
Jump to the top / bottom of whichever list or tab is active.
.TP
.B q / Ctrl\-C
Quit, from either the list or a detail view.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Normal exit, however the view was closed.
.TP
.B 1
The inventory couldn't be listed, it reported no hosts at all, or a
throwaway stub playbook this view depends on internally couldn't be
written.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR tangsible (1),
.BR tangsible-host (1)
